{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"42e2fa8521732ee576f2a2e3629491cf4d667ddf105ed8f7ee0a4370b92ea7af","digest":{"component_or_area":"opcert_service app and test infrastructure","key_entities":["src/rebar/opcert_service/app.py","tests/unit/test_opcert_service_app.py","test_matching_guard_is_accepted","asyncio.wait_for","asyncio.to_thread","_worker","lifespan","CPython issue 86296","commit 8c9bf5d78d","ADR-0067"],"problem_keywords":["pytest-xdist worker crash","flaky CI","asyncio cancellation","Python 3.11"],"propositions":["pytest-xdist worker process crashes (node down: Not properly terminated) on test_matching_guard_is_accepted intermittently on Python 3.11 in CI across random matrix shards","on Python 3.11, asyncio.wait_for consumes external cancellation when its child completes in the same event-loop turn, leaving the worker task in cancelling state and blocking lifespan shutdown","the crash is resolved by replacing asyncio.wait_for(asyncio.to_thread(...), timeout=…) with async with asyncio.timeout(...): await asyncio.to_thread(...) to restore correct cancellation semantics","Python 3.12+ is unaffected by the defect, and the failure is CI-only and load/timing-dependent due to the 3.11-specific asyncio cancellation bug"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787706393777280001,"uuid":"777a0f5e-52a0-4fad-bd6d-dcfea3fdbc7b"}